## E01 Twenty records from the open lists — QUEUED, next · Records · no strategy

Authority: owner direction 23 Oct 2026 ("combine the SEG open data list and the national
registers, verify the sources, show the real data"); this charter.

**Outcome.** The map lists at least twenty datasets. Each record states publisher, origin, access
mode, licence (name, redistribution, attribution) and kinds in the publisher's words, and each
origin was opened by a person on the day the record was written.

**Context today (verified 23 Oct, scaffold commit).** Nine records exist in `records/`
(equinor/volve, terranubis/f3-demo-2020, rmotc/teapot-dome, nopims/poseidon, nzpam/parihaka,
sodir/factpages, nlog/nlog, nsta/ndr, seg/open-data-wiki). `osd validate` passes. Licence
`redistribution` is `unknown` on five of them. The SEG wiki page cannot be fetched from the VPS
(HTTP 403, OSD-D9); it opens in an ordinary browser.

**The design the lane must map to.**
1. One record per dataset, never per file; a register (Sodir, NLOG, NDR, NOPIMS) is one record
   with `source-list` among its kinds plus one record per named dataset it carries that the SEG
   list names.
2. Candidates, in this order until twenty: the SEG open-data list entries whose origin still
   answers; Penobscot, Kerry 3D, Stratton, Groningen (NAM/NLOG), Netherlands F3 wells, Norne
   (NTNU), SEAM Phase I, Marmousi (synthetic, flagged in `notes`), Dutch and Danish (GEUS) registers,
   Geoscience Australia NOPIMS 3D surveys beyond Poseidon.
3. A dead origin is still a record: `known_issues` says "origin dead on <date>; last mirror
   <url>", and the record stays at L0. Dead links are the point of a verified list.
4. Licence fields: `unknown` when the publisher's page does not state it; never inferred from a
   country. `share_alike: true` whenever the licence is a BY-SA family.
5. Each record's `added` is the day the origin was opened by the author; the PR says who opened it.

**Acceptance.**
- `osd validate` reports `>= 20 records, 0 problems` (counted from `records/*/*.yaml`).
- Every record has `licence.redistribution` in {allowed, restricted, forbidden, unknown} and a
  `licence.url`; at most 8 of the twenty are `unknown` (hand count in the PR).
- `kinds` of every record intersect the Ophiolite E55 registry vocabulary (the schema enum).
- At least 12 records carry a `region.bbox` (the map's extent rectangles).
- The `verify` workflow comment on the PR lists every changed record with a level.
- Validity is three separate tests, each with a mutation, already in `tests/test_records.py`;
  the lane adds none unless the schema changes.

**Out of scope.** Outlines (E03), checksums (E02), mirrors (E07), any schema change (if one is
needed, stop and open a D item).

**Stop rules.** A publisher's page says redistribution is forbidden: record it, do not mirror,
continue. A licence page needs a login to read: `unknown`, note it, continue. More than three
candidates from the SEG list are dead: continue, they are records at L0.

**Ownership and dependencies.** Records lane; paths `records/**`. No dependency.

**Evidence to inspect.** `uv run osd status` output in the PR; the verify comment; a screenshot
of the map list showing the count.
## E08 Curation that runs itself — QUEUED · Surface · no strategy

Authority: `CONTRIBUTING.md`; analogues named 23 Oct (Registry of Open Data on AWS, conda-forge).

**Outcome.** An outside contributor's record merges the same day with one human reading the
licence fields; a dead origin becomes an issue with the date it died; a visitor sees when each
record was last verified and by what.

**Context today (verified 23 Oct).** `CONTRIBUTING.md`, a PR template and a dataset issue
template exist. The `verify` workflow comments levels on records PRs. No CODEOWNERS, no dead-link
report, no status page, no outside contribution yet.

**The design the lane must map to.**
1. `CODEOWNERS`: `records/**` to the records maintainers, `schema/**` and `src/**` to the kernel
   maintainers.
2. Dead-link report: a dispatch of `verify` over all records ends with one issue per record
   that fell from L1+ to L0 since the last stored result, titled "origin dead: <id>", with the
   HTTP class and date; blocked (403) never opens an issue (OSD-D9).
3. `site/status.html`: the `osd status` table with `checked_at`, sortable, from `records.json`.
4. A "Suggest a dataset" issue is turned into a record PR by a maintainer with `osd new <url>`,
   which scaffolds the YAML from the template and the page title.
5. First outside contribution: the lane asks two named people from the Software Underground
   community to add one record each and records the elapsed time from PR open to merge.

**Acceptance.**
- Two outside PRs merged, each under 24 h from open to merge (dates in the PR descriptions).
- A fixture run where one record's fetcher returns 404 after a stored L1 opens exactly one issue
  (dry-run output in the test).
- `status.html` lists every record with level and date (screenshot).
- `osd new https://example.org/x` writes a file that fails validation only on the fields a human
  must fill (test asserts the exact problem list).

**Out of scope.** Automated licence detection, scheduled runs (R6: on demand), moderation tooling.

**Stop rules.** No outside contributor answers within a week: record it, merge the rest, leave
the acceptance line open in PROGRAM.md rather than faking a contribution.

**Ownership and dependencies.** Coding lane; paths `.github/**` (announced), `site/status.html`,
`src/osd/new.py`, `src/osd/report.py`, `tests/test_report.py`. Depends on E02 (stored results).

**Evidence to inspect.** The two PR links; the status screenshot.
## E10 Seismic slices — DEFERRED · Kernel · strategy at lane open · one Codex round

Authority: owner direction 23 Oct ("only a slice from a 3D cube rather than the entire dataset");
Ophiolite E100 (ranged reads at a resolution).

**Outcome.** In a notebook, a person reads one inline, crossline or time slice of a mirrored
seismic volume through an HTTP byte-range read, without downloading the cube and without a
server of ours running.

**Context today (verified 23 Oct).** Nothing. E07 would hold mirrored SEG-Y, which cannot be
sliced without a full read. The analogue is Zarr over object storage (Pangeo); the subsurface
form is MDIO (Zarr-based) or OpenVDS (OSDU). Ophiolite reads ZGY (E123).

**The design the lane must map to.**
1. One chunked store format for mirrored volumes, Zarr-based, chosen at lane open with a
   measured comparison on F3 (file count, bytes, slice latency from the bucket): MDIO is the
   default candidate.
2. Conversion is an E07 mirror step with a fidelity check: 100 random traces compared sample by
   sample to the SEG-Y original, zero differences.
3. Reader: `osd.seismic.open(item_id)` returns an xarray-like object; a slice reads only the
   chunks it needs (asserted by counting HTTP requests in the test).
4. Cost line: bytes stored per volume and egress per slice, by hand, in the PR.

**Acceptance.**
- A time slice of F3 from the bucket completes in under 3 s on the VPS and issues fewer than
  (volume chunks / 10) range requests.
- The fidelity check passes on F3 and fails on a fixture with one altered sample (mutation).
- The notebook in `examples/` runs top to bottom in CI against a local store.

**Out of scope.** Hosted compute, interpretation, anything beyond slicing.

**Stop rules.** F3's licence (CC BY-SA) requires the converted store to carry the same licence:
record it in custody; if any candidate volume is `redistribution: unknown`, it is not converted.

**Ownership and dependencies.** Coding lane; paths `src/osd/seismic/**`, `examples/**`, tests.
Depends on E07 and OSD-D6. Deferred until E07 is merged and a second volume with `allowed` exists.

**Evidence to inspect.** The comparison table at lane open; the request count; the cost line.
## E11 Hosting and domain — IN PROGRESS · Ops · no strategy

Authority: `DECISIONS.md` OSD-D1 (public repository), OSD-D4 (opensubsurfacedata.org, bought at
Spaceship 23 Oct), OSD-D5 (results on a branch, bucket only for mirrors).

**Outcome.** The site answers at https://opensubsurfacedata.org with real verification levels,
and nothing about hosting needs a secret.

**Context today (23 Oct).** Repository public at `ophiolite-labs/open-subsurface-data`; `pages.yml`
publishes `site/` on every merge and reads the `verification-results` branch that a dispatched
`verify` run force-pushes. GitHub Pages serves from the github.io address until DNS points at it.

**The design the lane must map to.**
1. Apex `opensubsurfacedata.org` on GitHub Pages: four A and four AAAA records at Spaceship, a
   `www` CNAME to `ophiolite-labs.github.io`, the custom domain set on the repository's Pages
   settings, HTTPS enforced once the certificate is issued.
2. Domain verified for the ophiolite-labs organisation (a TXT record) so no other account can
   claim the name on Pages.
3. Verification results: the `verification-results` branch; no bucket, no key.
4. No analytics, no cookies; a plain `robots.txt` that allows indexing.
5. Mirrors (E07) get a bucket in a separate Hetzner project when that lane opens; nothing here.

**Acceptance.**
- `curl -sI https://opensubsurfacedata.org/` returns 200; `http://` redirects to `https://`.
- `www.opensubsurfacedata.org` redirects to the apex.
- After a dispatched verify run, the published `data/records.json` shows `L1` for
  `sodir/factpages` with that run's date.
- `dig TXT _github-pages-challenge-ophiolite-labs.opensubsurfacedata.org` returns the value the
  organisation settings show.

**Out of scope.** CDN beyond Pages, mirrors, uptime monitoring.

**Stop rules.** DNS not yet entered: everything else is done; the domain lines wait on the owner.

**Ownership and dependencies.** Supervisor; paths `.github/workflows/**`, `site/robots.txt`,
`docs/program/**`. Owner actions: the DNS records and the TXT record.

**Evidence to inspect.** The curl and dig outputs; the published `records.json`.
## E12 Catalogue into a workspace — DEFERRED · Kernel, cross-repo · strategy at lane open · one Codex round

Authority: owner direction 23 Oct ("pull references of that data into their private workspace …
read-only access … derive products … push back"); Ophiolite E72a (source bindings), E73/E65
(fixed address per version), E69 (versions), E36/E79/E80 (where a person's workspace runs).

**Outcome.** A person binds a catalogue collection to their Ophiolite project as a read-only
source, works on a curve or a slice without copying the dataset, derives a new asset and keeps it
in their own project with provenance pointing at the catalogue item and version. The read is
intentional (check, get), nothing updates itself.

**Context today (23 Oct, from program memory; verify at lane open).** Ophiolite source bindings
exist for connected databases (E39–E42) and remote sources (E100a's Workspace remote source);
E36 public tenancy is deferred; E79 gives a local instance, E80 an own instance. Cross-instance
binding does not exist and is out of scope here: the catalogue is static HTTP, so any instance
can read it.

**The design the lane must map to.**
1. A catalogue collection is a source kind in Ophiolite ("Open Subsurface Data"), bound by the
   STAC collection address; items are read on demand through E06's manifest reader and, for
   curves, E100's ranged reads over mirrored files.
2. Derived assets are ordinary E69 versions whose E122 provenance names catalogue item id and
   `catalog_version`; "check" compares `catalog_version` and shows what changed, applies nothing.
3. Rights follow E09's mapping; a derived asset from a share-alike item inherits the licence in
   its rights-basis.
4. Where it runs: the E79 try-it instance first (no hosted sign-up needed), E80 second, hosted
   when E36 lands.

**Acceptance (frozen at lane open from the Ophiolite journey fixtures, by hand).**
- Bind F3, open one well's gamma-ray curve through a ranged read (request count below the
  file's chunk count), run a notebook cell that derives a smoothed curve, save it: the new
  version's provenance names the F3 item id and the catalogue commit.
- Change the catalogue fixture's commit: "check" lists F3 as changed; nothing in the project moves.
- A derived asset from F3 shows CC-BY-SA-4.0 in its rights-basis; one from Teapot Dome shows
  public domain with no attribution requirement.

**Out of scope.** Cross-instance bindings, hosted compute next to the data, seismic beyond E10.

**Stop rules.** Ophiolite E36 and E79 both unavailable to the lane: stop, the epic stays
deferred.

**Ownership and dependencies.** One Ophiolite lane (chartered in the Ophiolite program) and a small
lane here for whatever the reader needs. Depends on E09, E10 for slices, and Ophiolite E36 or E79.

**Evidence to inspect.** The Ophiolite journey test; the provenance record; the rights-basis views.

